ex:IA10_NoAnalogies a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR10_NoAnalogies ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Decision made by me, not asked, because the Owner's own ruling and the lineage 11 precedent settle it: the analogy slides stay as slides (same count, titles of four words or more) and say plainly what each concept is and does, with the box label IN SHORT, as in chapters 10 and 11. The open question on the chapter 17 main-thread budget is not touched by this change." ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (2026-11-25, read-only, from 08-tooling/ch17-deck/spec_v3_0_0/content_v3_0_0.py): the chapter 17 deck has 12 analogy slides titled Everyday pictures with 83 concept lines, a summary sentence that compares a summary to a packing list and a practice sentence that compares practice to finger scales; the notes file notes_v3_0_0.py has 28 lines with comparison wording to read. NOT YET MEASURED and stated: the chapter 17 lecture text and code source, and everything of chapter 16 (its deck is the old 1.0.0 file; its spec is not written, so it is written plain from the start). IMPACT: the slide count stays 59; the rule of the mission that content stays as approved is met with one stated exception, the analogy lines; the page of chapter 17 waits for the plain deck, which re-ranks TK10_Page_17_Build behind it." ;
    backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage10 ;
    rdfs:label "Where the analogies are in chapter 17 today, measured before planning"@en .
ex:Lineage10 a backlog:Lineage ; backlog:lineageArchived true ; backlog:hasArchivalConfirmationStatus backlog:AC_PendingConfirmation ;
    backlog:continuesFrom ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:followsProfileDeclaration ex:ProfileDecl10 ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Chapter 17 page stage 2026-11-20: page 9.20.0 (deck 3.0.0 manifest, lambda-free A-box 1.0.4 in the form the browser runs, inputs renamed to 9_20_0, drafts 9.32-9.96 removed). Root causes found and fixed: examples were built with the wrong Python (now the browser's Pyodide); the interpreter wrapper treated sys.exit(0) as failure; the first picture example paid about 250 ms for loading all Pillow plugins (now three plugins loaded at start); one example, Decrypt return values, tried five passwords at about 35 ms each (now three; the other two cases stay covered by two other examples). Remaining: the post-load main-thread check measures 222 to 309 ms against 200 ms because each example run takes 120 to 250 ms on this two-core machine; the same examples took the same time in the earlier page here. Not weakened, not waived: page stage not Done, release stage not opened. Owner decision requested."@en ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Owner decision 2026-11-20: for the queued lab lineage, each lab session follows one book chapter and is built from that chapter's own practice projects and exercises on GitHub; course outcomes are checked afterwards as coverage at most. Recorded only; the lab lineage is not opened." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Owner note 2026-11-20 (11:04): the lab content is to be discussed with the owner before any work, and must use the book's resources where they are available on GitHub (the 3rd-edition book ontology package and this repository's textbook and assessment records) rather than ad hoc material. Recorded against the queued lab lineage; nothing written for it." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Routing 2026-11-20 (G195): the owner asked for a lab-materials package (lab handouts, quizzes with answers, one interactive HTML page per session, reusable by any Python course; repository to follow). It does not serve this lineage's mission and is not urgent, so route (c): queued as the next lineage, opened only after this lineage is concluded and the owner confirms; no file of the package was written. The owner chose this route over closing this lineage as partial or declaring an urgency." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Urgency 2026-11-20 17:37 Istanbul: the Owner opened an urgency case on the chapter 10 and 11 slides and code examples. Routed under step 3g(b) of the lineage discipline (read live from GitHub, v163.0.7): declared first, the urgent work in a lineage of its own, built after the declaration. Governing OE rules read from the latest governance ABox: plain talk with the Owner (BP-D63), verify before shipping (L-65), act when the evidence decides (L-78), every named objection gets its own answer (L-113). The chapter 17 page stage (410 of 412 checks, one speed check open) is untouched and waits; the open question on it stays with the Owner." ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Achieved ;
    backlog:hasProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ;
    backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission10 ;
    backlog:lineageOrdinal "10"^^xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "ex:Lineage2 (sen0414-slides-lineage namespace) is the closed slides lineage this continues from, as Lineage3 to Lineage9 do."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 16 and 17 corrections, narrow lineage"@en .
